# Code With Rahim — Portfolio (Next.js)

Modern, fully responsive portfolio website built with **Next.js 15**, **TypeScript**,
**Tailwind CSS**, and **SQLite** (via better-sqlite3). Works on desktop, tablet,
and mobile out of the box, and deploys to **Vercel directly from GitHub**.

## Features

- **Public site** — home (hero, services, featured projects, about, experience timeline, contact form), projects page, resume page, and admin-created dynamic pages
- **Admin panel** (`/admin`) — dashboard with analytics, projects/services/skills/experience/pages content management, messages inbox, and site settings editor
- **Contact form** — messages saved to the database; optional email delivery via Resend
- **Page-view analytics** — lightweight traffic tracking with a weekly views chart
- **Fully responsive** — mobile-first layouts with a mobile navigation menu
- **Seeded starter content** — the site looks complete on first run; edit everything from the admin

## Tech Stack

- Next.js 15 (App Router) + React 19 + TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS v4
- better-sqlite3 (SQLite database at `data/site.db`)
- Font Awesome + Google Fonts (Sora / Inter)

## Local Development

Requires Node.js 20+ (Bun or npm).

```bash
bun install
bun run dev        # http://localhost:3000
```

Other scripts: `bun run build` (production build), `bun run start` (serve build),
`bun run typecheck` (TypeScript check).

### Admin login

The admin password defaults to `admin12345` in development. In production you MUST
set the `ADMIN_PASSWORD` environment variable — without it the admin login is
disabled.

## Deploy on Vercel (via GitHub)

1. Push this repository to GitHub.
2. Go to [vercel.com](https://vercel.com) → **Add New → Project** → import the GitHub repo.
3. Vercel auto-detects Next.js — the default build (`next build`) works as-is. Click **Deploy**.
4. Add the environment variables below under **Project → Settings → Environment Variables**.

### Environment variables

| Variable | Required | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `ADMIN_PASSWORD` | Production | Admin panel password (required in production) |
| `CONTACT_EMAIL` | Optional | Email address that receives contact form notifications |
| `RESEND_API_KEY` | Optional | Resend API key — enables email delivery for the contact form |
| `EMAIL_FROM` | Optional | Sender address for contact emails (default: Resend onboarding) |
| `SOCIAL_GITHUB` / `SOCIAL_LINKEDIN` / `SOCIAL_TWITTER` / `SOCIAL_INSTAGRAM` / `SOCIAL_FACEBOOK` | Optional | Social profile URLs shown in the footer and contact section |

### Database note

The app stores content in a local SQLite file (`data/site.db`). On Vercel this file
is created at runtime and is **ephemeral** — it resets on redeploys and cold starts.
For persistent storage (recommended for production contact messages), the data layer
can be swapped to PostgreSQL — say the word and this repo can be wired to Neon +
Prisma while keeping the same pages.

## Project Structure

```
app/            Next.js App Router pages (public + admin)
components/     Reusable React components (navbar, footer, forms, admin UI)
lib/            Data layer (db.ts, site.ts), auth, and email helpers
data/           SQLite database file (gitignored)
public/images/  Site images
```
